Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 09:05:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] build: bump ctutils (#49187)

Current main seem to
```
  | /home/jane/dev/servo/deny.toml:169: Non-constant-time mask generation and `u128` comparisons: ctutils 0.4.3 registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index
```

so I did
```
cargo update -p ctutils --precise 0.4.4
```

and it updated a sole dependency
after update, the error is gone

Fixes
[RUSTSEC-2026-0385](https://rustsec.org/advisories/RUSTSEC-2026-0385.html)

Checked for no PRs addressing it yet

Testing: `./mach test-tidy`

Signed-off-by: Asset Malik <5373400+janeoa@users.noreply.github.com>
(cherry picked from commit 7615ccf8186b57ef57f96b35b8ff7cc571f8da54)

----

Fork note: backport of upstream 7615ccf8186 (#49187), which landed after
base/2026-10-22. RustSec published RUSTSEC-2026-0385 for ctutils 0.4.3,
so `cargo-deny` in `./mach test-tidy` failed on ohos-main. The next
commit, the backport of e78fc913f26, moves ctutils on to 0.4.5, as
upstream did.
Drop at the next sync: every later base contains 7615ccf8186, so this
commit applies empty and becomes a `Superseded-by: 7615ccf8186`
placeholder (runbook decision 3).

Validation: `./mach test-tidy` on ohos-main bf7c1c76aff fails in `cargo-deny` with RUSTSEC-2026-0387 (crypto-bigint 0.7.5) and RUSTSEC-2026-0385 (ctutils 0.4.3), as the Lint job of every pull request would; with both backports it passes, and `cargo-deny check` reports advisories, bans, licenses and sources ok. Same patch-id as upstream (`git patch-id --stable`). With both, on top of patch 130: `./mach clippy --locked -- -- --deny warnings`, `RUSTFLAGS="-D warnings" ./mach build --use-crown --locked --profile checked-release`, the same build with `--ohos` (the Rust part; packaging then stops at the local signing configuration), and `./mach test-unit --profile checked-release` (1,255 tests) and `--doc` (46) pass.
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; the agent cherry-picked upstream commit 7615ccf8186 without changes and added the fork-style part of this message below the dashed line: fork note, Validation and these trailers)
Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
